WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 line:92%
-I'm very glad you're here.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:04.037 size:81% position:41%
I want to talk about
"The Disaster Artist,"

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I loved, and want
to get to the Golden Globes.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, one of the things that
happened at the Golden Globes,

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:10.910
and obviously, this happened
in the last couple of days

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
before we had
you booked on the show

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.780 line:92%
and I'm glad you're still here.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were wearing a Time's Up
button like a lot of guys

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the show and some women
during your time on stage said

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.788
that was hypocritical, they went
to Twitter and said that

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:24.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was hypocritical based on
their experiences that

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have had with you.
They made some allegations.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:30.463
I wonder if you have read
those tweets, and if so,

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.633 size:88% position:44% line:92%
how you respond to them?

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was sent a couple
of the tweets, so yeah,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I did read them.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.641 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I haven't responded.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:46.846
I think -- Well, the ones
I read were not accurate,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:51.484
but one of the things that
I've learned is that this is

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
a conversation that
obviously needs to be had.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:59.659
There are people, women and
others, who have not been a part

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.629 size:78% position:39%
of this conversation,
and I truly believe

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.932
and why I was wearing the pin is
that they need to be a part

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:10.003 size:81% position:41%
of this conversation,
and so I support that.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.939 line:92%
-Ally Sheedy also had a tweet.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.007 line:92%
She has since took it down.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
I heard you mention last night
on Stephen Colbert's show

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you had directed
her in a play.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've had a good experience
with her.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.483 size:75% position:38%
Have you reached out
to her as someone --

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:27.087
And, are you not curious
as to why she would do that

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you had,
from your perspective,

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.890 line:92%
a good relationship with her?

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I had a great --
I had a great relationship

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.662 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with her.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
She took the tweet down,
I don't know.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really don't.
-Not curious enough, though,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
to reach out to her as someone
that you've had

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.505
a good relationship with before
and to try to understand why

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
she would have done that?
-[ Sighs ]

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
I -- [ Sighs ]

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was so shocking.
I don't know.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:57.283
I just --
I guess I'm just letting it be.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:00.153
-The last thing I'll say,
or ask about this, I should say,

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:04.524
this moment, you know, I think
this is an exciting time because

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:07.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's allowing us all remember,
especially as men,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there were other people
in different perspectives

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.731 line:92%
for things that we experienced.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:15.135
Does this Time's Up movement
and this moment we're having

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:18.071
right now, does it make you
look back at all and question

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.873 size:75% position:38%
any of your behavior
in the past based on

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
this new perspective
we're getting on how women

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
have perceived things
for so long?

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:28.948
-I think what I really learned
and being here and this week

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that show that we were --
You know.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-I mean, it was so powerful

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:33.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
in there.
-That we heard some

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
amazing things from
some amazing women.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:42.395
-Like I said, there are stories
that need to get out.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:46.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are people
that need to be heard.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:52.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have my own side of
this story, but I believe in,

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:56.342
you know, these people that have
been underrepresented getting

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.711 size:88% position:44%
their stories out enough
that I will, you know,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:02.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
hold back things that
I could say just because

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.349 line:92%
I believe in it that much.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if I have to take a knock
because I'm not going to,

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:11.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, try and, you know,
actively refute things,

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
then I will, because I believe
in it that much.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I want to also move on
to the film you made...

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:17.931 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:20.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and thank you for speaking
to me about those things.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.602 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I really appreciate it.

